course: dictionary
lesson: 9564
title: Straightener and the clues around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A straightener is a thing that makes something straight. You may already know the word, but in a text it can also mean a hot tool that makes hair straight. The words around it give you the clues. «Hair straighteners get very hot, so they are switched off and put on a heat mat.» The words very hot tell you this is a tool that needs care.
explain: Hair straighteners have two flat plates. You close them on hair and pull them down, and the curls or waves turn straight. A text may not explain how they work, so you can use your own picture of a flat iron and the word straight to build the meaning.
explain: Context also tells you what to do. Words like switched off, heat mat and unplug show that a straightener is safe only when it is handled properly. Always ask: what does this sentence want me to know? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it makes sense.
fact: A straightener is a thing that makes something straight.
fact: Hair straighteners are a hot electric tool with two flat plates.
fact: Hair straighteners are used to make curly or wavy hair straight.
fact: Straighteners get very hot, so they can burn skin or start a fire.
fact: Unplug them after use and keep them away from small children.
exercise: «Hair straighteners get very hot, so they are switched off and put on a heat mat.» What is a straightener? | A kind of hat | A thing that makes something curly | A cold drink | *A thing that makes something straight
exercise: Hair straighteners have two flat plates. What are they used for? | Cutting paper into shapes | Cooking eggs for breakfast | *Making curly or wavy hair straight | Curling hair into tight ringlets
exercise: Why should you unplug hair straighteners after you use them? | They run out of battery | They will stop working if they get cold | *They get very hot and can burn skin or start a fire | They make the room smell of soap
test: «Hair straighteners get very hot, so they are switched off.» Which word tells you they must be handled with care? | Hair | *Very hot | Switched | Straighteners
test: Which is the usual plural form of straightener? | straightenes | straightener's | *straighteners | straightenerses
exam: Dina says hair straighteners are a cold tool for curly hair. What is wrong with her idea? | *They are hot, and they are used to straighten hair, not curl it | They are cold, and they are used to curl hair | They are plates of metal for the kitchen | They are only used on children
